event: response.reasoning_summary_text.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","item_id":"rs_0777d83ef76b48ae016acba28f99888190afa17736ec378ab1","output_index":0,"sequence_number":91,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Preparing memory seed insert**\n\nI’m thinking about how to implement table memory seed inserts while ignoring each startup position from tasks. This involves creating a transaction record and then executing updates atomically. I wonder if I can eliminate the tasks.position or if it’s better to keep it mirrored. I also want to create a prepared insert for the maximum memory and record it through a wrapper transaction. It seems like I've got enough time to figure out the helper transaction synchronously."}

